        <briefdescription>
<para>This implements an analogous, but entirely distinct transform from the main loop predication transform. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This one is phrased in terms of using a widenable branch <emphasis>outside</emphasis> the loop to allow us to simplify loop exits in a following loop. This is close in spirit to the IndVarSimplify transform of the same name, but is materially different widening loosens legality sharply. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Here we can be fairly sure that executing this exit will most likely lead to executing llvm.experimental.deoptimize. This is a profitability heuristic, not a legality constraint.</para>
        </inbodydescription>
